  body: '<b>CHAD "THE CODE WIZARD" THUNDERSON</b>

    Applying for: Junior Gameplay
    Programmer (overqualified)


    <b>EXPERIENCE</b>

    {title}

    {dates}


    <b>SKILLS</b>

    {skill_html}

    {skill_years}


    <b>ACHIEVEMENTS</b>

    {invented}


    <b>REFERENCES</b>

    {ref}'
  claims:
  - id: title
    text: Founder, CEO & Supreme Coder - ThunderCorp
    isSuspicious: 1
    category: 2
    designerNote: 
    suspiciousQuestion:
      question: '''Supreme Coder'' at ThunderCorp. How many employees does ThunderCorp
        have?'
      answer: Including me? {c_one}. But {c_dog} is basically an employee.
      demeanor: 1
      phrases:
      - id: c_one
        text: One
        isContradiction: 0
        callOutResponse: One is a number of employees. And that number is mine.
        callOutDemeanor: 1
      - id: c_dog
        text: my dog Byte
        isContradiction: 0
        callOutResponse: Byte handles QA. He has found zero bugs. Flawless record.
        callOutDemeanor: 1
    goodQuestion:
      question: Founder and CEO! What does ThunderCorp make?
      answer: Vibes, mostly. And one app. It's a flashlight. It doesn't turn off.
      demeanor: 1
      phrases: []
  - id: dates
    text: Jan 2025 - Dec 2031
    isSuspicious: 1
    category: 1
    designerNote: Future end date breaks rule 2.
    suspiciousQuestion:
      question: Your job ends in 2031. That is in the future.
      answer: I {f_plan} ahead. I signed a six-year contract. With myself.
      demeanor: 4
      phrases:
      - id: f_plan
        text: plan
        isContradiction: 0
        callOutResponse: Visionaries plan. You wouldn't understand. No offense.
        callOutDemeanor: 4
    goodQuestion:
      question: A six-year commitment. Love the loyalty.
      answer: Thank you. I'm extremely loyal. To myself.
      demeanor: 1
      phrases: []
  - id: skill_html
    text: HTML (expert programming language)
    isSuspicious: 1
    category: 4
    designerNote: 
    suspiciousQuestion:
      question: You listed HTML as a programming language.
      answer: Yes. It's the {h_power}. Everything on the internet is HTML.
      demeanor: 4
      phrases:
      - id: h_power
        text: most powerful programming language
        isContradiction: 0
        callOutResponse: Name one website without HTML. Exactly. You can't.
        callOutDemeanor: 4
    goodQuestion:
      question: HTML expert! Great.
      answer: I once made a website that was just the word 'Chad' in bold. It got
        four visits. All me.
      demeanor: 1
      phrases: []
  - id: skill_years
    text: 40 years of Unity 6 experience
    isSuspicious: 1
    category: 4
    designerNote: 'Impossible: Unity 6 is from 2024.'
    suspiciousQuestion:
      question: Unity 6 came out in 2024. How do you have 40 years of experience
        with it?
      answer: I {u_parallel}. Ten projects at once, four years each. Math.
      demeanor: 1
      phrases:
      - id: u_parallel
        text: work in parallel
        isContradiction: 0
        callOutResponse: Have you heard of multitasking? I invented it.
        callOutDemeanor: 1
    goodQuestion:
      question: 40 years with Unity 6. You must be the best in the world.
      answer: I am. I'm also {u_age}. Not related.
      demeanor: 1
      phrases:
      - id: u_age
        text: 24 years old
        isContradiction: 1
        callOutResponse: ...Okay, it's more like 40 HOURS. But they were very intense
          hours.
        callOutDemeanor: 3
  - id: invented
    text: Invented the semicolon (2019)
    isSuspicious: 1
    category: 0
    designerNote: 
    suspiciousQuestion:
      question: You invented the semicolon in 2019?
      answer: Before me, code just {s_ran}. Total chaos. You're welcome.
      demeanor: 5
      phrases:
      - id: s_ran
        text: ran together like one long sentence
        isContradiction: 0
        callOutResponse: Look it up. Actually, don't look it up.
        callOutDemeanor: 5
    goodQuestion:
      question: Inventing the semicolon is a big deal.
      answer: It was a big year. I also invented the {s_comma}.
      demeanor: 1
      phrases:
      - id: s_comma
        text: comma
        isContradiction: 0
        callOutResponse: And the period. Punctuation is my passion.
        callOutDemeanor: 1
  - id: ref
    text: Brenda Thunderson (Mom)
    isSuspicious: 1
    category: 5
    designerNote: Family reference breaks rule 3.
    suspiciousQuestion:
      question: Your reference is your mom.
      answer: She's also my manager. She signs my {m_report}.
      demeanor: 4
      phrases:
      - id: m_report
        text: report card
        isContradiction: 1
        callOutResponse: My PERFORMANCE review. It has gold stars on it. I'm a professional.
        callOutDemeanor: 3
    goodQuestion:
      question: Honestly, moms are great references.
      answer: Thank you! She says I'm {m_special}.
      demeanor: 1
      phrases:
      - id: m_special
        text: very special
        isContradiction: 0
        callOutResponse: She says it every day. Sometimes with a sigh, but she says
          it.
        callOutDemeanor: 1
